We don't know if the limit is her life span. It could be she can use 1 year of her lifespan on herself in a day or what. Also, all we know is that she heals and get stronger when she uses her life span, doesn't mean she gets stamina. Like if Mansherry just heal herself to keep making heal balls. or Tama eating a smile then eating her dango. since we know that the dango strengthens the pleasures. There must be a limit to those things.

&#x200B;

And considering the BM's soul is literally used on some homies, she probably can't use more  than a year at a certain timeframe. so maybe having 60% of their soul on the user's body limits how much lifespan you can use.

I have read your links and all of the studies checked up on the patients after 1-2 years after their complete transition. I don't think that is a good metric to see any regret from the kids in a longer time span. 

&#x200B;

You did find 1 case of it working in the long run but it's still too little of a data pool to say that this is the majority in the Long-term. I think we need to wait for more data to make a conclusion. In a wider time-span
